        <div id="amazon" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Can You Buy Sam's Club Protein Powder on Amazon?
          </h2>

          <p>
            You can buy every name-brand powder Sam's stocks on Amazon, but not in the same sizes and rarely at the same price, and the Member's Mark shake is not sold there at all. Member's Mark is Sam's Club's own label, so anything with that name on Amazon is a third-party reseller listing, usually at a markup and with uncertain storage history.
          </p>

          <p>
            For the name brands, Amazon is the convenient option rather than the cheap one. The 5 lb Gold Standard tub we saw at $100.67 works out to about $1.44 per 25 g, more than double the member deal price reported at Sam's. Muscle Milk Genuine's 4.94 lb tub at $59.29 came to about $1.45 per 25 g, close to Sam's listed price for the smaller tub. RAW isolate and Orgain were both cheaper per gram at their Sam's prices than on Amazon.
          </p>

          <p>
            For the Member's Mark shake, the closest Amazon alternative is Premier Protein's 30 g shake, which has the same 30 g of protein and 160 calories per bottle. At $25.49 for a 12-pack of 11 oz bottles, it costs about $1.77 per 25 g, more than the Member's Mark price buyers reported. Our <a href="/muscle-milk-vs-premier-protein/">Muscle Milk vs Premier Protein</a> comparison covers both brands' shakes side by side.
          </p>

          <p>
            Our advice: if you hold a Sam's card and live near a club, buy Gold Standard, RAW and Orgain there. If you do not, buy on Amazon in the largest size you will finish, use Subscribe and Save where offered, and compare the cost per 25 g with the cheapest options in our <a href="/best-cheap-protein-powder/">cheap protein powder rankings</a> before checking out.
          </p>
        </div>

