        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming Member's Mark makes a protein powder</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Sam's own label currently makes a 30 g ready-to-drink shake, not a powder. Older blog posts and resellers can blur that line. If you see a Member's Mark tub online, check the seller, the label and the date before buying, because a reseller listing may be old stock at a markup.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing tub prices instead of cost per 25 g</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A $30 tub and a $50 bag are not comparable until you divide by servings and protein per serving. Muscle Milk Genuine's $30.48 tub costs more per gram than a $49.98 Gold Standard bag, despite the smaller sticker price. Do the per-25 g math on your phone in the aisle.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying a membership only for protein</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                At $60 a year for Club, Sam's only pays off on powder if you drink shakes often and catch member deals. Someone using a tub every two months may save less than the fee. Price the same products at Walmart and Aldi, which charge nothing to walk in.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating every Sam's powder as third-party tested</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Only some brands publish certifications: Muscle Milk is NSF Certified for Sport per the brand, and ON says Gold Standard is banned-substance tested. RAW's listing names no certifier and Orgain publishes none. Drug-tested athletes should check the certifier's database for the exact flavor and lot.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the biggest bag in an untried flavor</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A 5.47 or 5.64 lb bag is about 80 shakes. If you dislike the flavor, the low cost per gram is wasted. Try a small tub of the same flavor first, or stick to the flavors buyers rate most often, such as Gold Standard's chocolate options, before committing to a warehouse size.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

