        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            12. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="faq-list">
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Sam's Club protein powder third-party tested?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  It depends on the brand, because Sam's Club has no house powder and does not certify products itself. Muscle Milk is listed by the brand as NSF Certified for Sport. Optimum Nutrition calls Gold Standard banned-substance tested and promotes Informed Choice on many flavors. RAW's isolate listing names no certifier, and Orgain publishes no sport certification. Check the certifier's database for your exact flavor.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Sam's Club sell a Member's Mark protein powder?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Not that we could find as of November 2026. Sam's Club's protein powder aisle is name brands such as Optimum Nutrition, Muscle Milk, RAW, Dymatize and Orgain. The only Member's Mark protein product we found is a 30 g high-protein chocolate shake in 18-packs of 11 oz bottles, with 160 calories and 1 g of sugar per bottle, per the Sam's listing.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Sam's Club protein powder healthy?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The main powders are ordinary, reasonably clean products. Gold Standard gives 24 g of protein in about 120 calories; Orgain is organic plant protein with no added sugar; RAW is a low-fat whey isolate. Muscle Milk Genuine has about 270 to 280 calories per serving, which suits weight gain more than dieting. People with kidney disease or other conditions should ask a doctor first.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Sam's Club protein powder contain dairy or lactose?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Most of it does. Gold Standard, RAW isolate and Muscle Milk are milk-based, and the Member's Mark shake lists milk protein concentrate. Isolate such as RAW has less lactose than concentrate but is not lactose-free. Orgain's organic plant protein is the dairy-free choice Sam's reliably stocks. Anyone with a milk allergy should avoid the dairy products entirely.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What is the cheapest protein powder at Sam's Club?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard is usually the cheapest per gram when Sam's runs its member price near the $49.98 that deal posters have reported for the 5.47 and 5.64 lb bags. That works out to about $0.65 per 25 g. Muscle Milk Genuine, listed at $30.48 for 2.47 lb, is about $1.49 per 25 g. Prices change, so check the app.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Which flavor is best at Sam's Club?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Buyers most often recommend Gold Standard's chocolate flavors, including the Extreme Milk Chocolate that Sam's sells in the 5.64 lb bag, and Vanilla Ice Cream as a mixer for smoothies. RAW buyers tend to favor its dessert-style flavors. Orgain buyers are split: some like the vanilla bean, others find the chocolate gritty. These reflect buyer reviews, not our tasting.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What are the common complaints about protein powder at Sam's Club?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The main complaints in Sam's buyer reviews are hidden prices online, tubs that look half full on opening, recipe changes and texture. One Muscle Milk Genuine reviewer reported a changed formula and grainy texture; some Orgain buyers call it gritty; a RAW buyer questioned the serving count. Stock also varies by club, so a product online may be missing in store.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

          </div>
